  "step_2": "The verbal report consists of the German phrase 'höherer Gewinn', which translates to 'higher win' or 'higher gain'. This indicates that the individual focused on the maximum possible outcome of the lotteries. The highest gain in Lottery B is 2500€, which is higher than the 2400€ in Lottery A. The individual appears to justify their choice by referencing this higher potential reward. There is no mention of probabilities, distributions, skewness, or unfavorable outcomes. The justification is solely outcome-based, emphasizing the top prize.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on assessing the skewness of the lottery distributions, particularly the concentration of probability on unfavorable outcomes, and prefers the more right-skewed option (Lottery B). However, the individual’s reasoning, as expressed in the verbal report, focuses exclusively on the higher possible gain (2500€ vs 2400€), showing no indication of considering the distribution of probabilities or the concept of skewness. While both the reason and the individual might end up favoring Lottery B, the justification processes are entirely different: one is distribution-based (skewness), the other is outcome-based (maximum payoff). There is no evidence that the individual considered the probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes or compared the shapes of the distributions. Therefore, it is unlikely that the skewness-based reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
